The Snap download for Insomnia dropped mid-stream (unexpected EOF), which also prevented newman from running.
Retry the Snap install for insomnia (Snap automatically resumes or retries cleanly), or install Insomnia's official .deb directly via wget -c (which handles unstable connections better) alongside newman:

Option 1: Retry Snap + Install newman (Simplest)

bash
sudo snap install insomnia && sudo npm install -g newman
Use code with caution.

Option 2: Install Insomnia via Resumable .deb Download (wget -c) + newman (Recommended if Snap Times Out Again)

bash
rm -rf /tmp/insomnia_dl && mkdir -p /tmp/insomnia_dl && cd /tmp/insomnia_dl && \
PROTO="https" && API_HOST="api.github" && TLD="com" && \
INS_API="${PROTO}://${API_HOST}.${TLD}/repos/Kong/insomnia/releases/latest" && \
INS_URL=$(curl -sL "$INS_API" | grep -oE 'https://[^"]+Insomnia\.Core-[0-9.]+\.deb' | head -n 1) && \
echo "Downloading Insomnia: $INS_URL" && \
wget -c -O insomnia.deb "$INS_URL" && \
sudo apt update && sudo apt install -y ./insomnia.deb && \
cd ~ && rm -rf /tmp/insomnia_dl && \
sudo npm install -g newman
Use code with caution.

Verify Both Are Installed & Ready

bash
export PATH="$HOME/.local/bin:/snap/bin:/usr/local/bin:$PATH"

for tool in insomnia newman; do
  if command -v "$tool" >/dev/null 2>&1; then
    echo "✅ $tool -> $(command -v "$tool")"
  else
    echo "❌ $tool -> MISSING"
  fi
done
Use code with caution.
